From: AztecBot <tech@aztec-labs.com>
Date: Wed, 7 Oct 2026 23:38:31 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] test: re-derive the handshake fixture's recipient with the v3
 separator

RecipientSignature::verify opens by binding the returned keys to the address:
assert_eq(recipient, AztecAddress::compute(public_keys, partial_address)). The
fixture's recipient was derived under the old separator, so seven of the eight
recipient_signature tests fail on that line - every one that gets past it. The
schnorr signature is over [chain_id, version, registry, eph_pk_x] and does not
commit to the address, so only this constant moves.

Recomputing with the old separator reproduces the pinned value exactly, which
is what pins down the derivation inputs.

diff --git a/noir-projects/noir-contracts/contracts/standard/handshake_registry_contract/src/recipient_signature.nr b/noir-projects/noir-contracts/contracts/standard/handshake_registry_contract/src/recipient_signature.nr
index 9e8ab5192c6d32b3b071d53c6bee547b4d6950f6..1910167547862a0e060a574ceb8dc1833fce5586 100644
--- a/noir-projects/noir-contracts/contracts/standard/handshake_registry_contract/src/recipient_signature.nr
+++ b/noir-projects/noir-contracts/contracts/standard/handshake_registry_contract/src/recipient_signature.nr
@@ -168,7 +168,7 @@ mod test {
             ),
         };
         let recipient = AztecAddress::from_field(
-            0x1b94108a8172e103629879215c11f224522aa1bd0e4d50505c041c500f82d15b,
+            0x1866b3a27833a08ad11e6a93fc45227aca73ef01e8df719a11f078ab9bfef2c4,
         );
         let chain_id = 0x7a69;
         let version = 1;
